quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  95,1,"By the fig and the olive,"
  95,2,"by Mount Sinai,"
  95,3,by this secure city (of Mecca):
  95,4,"We, indeed, created human being in the most beautiful form,"
  95,5,"then, We returned him to the lowest of the low,"
  95,6,except those who believe and perform righteous deeds. They will have a never-ending reward.
  95,7,"So, (after knowing this) what makes you deny the Retribution?"
  95,8,Is not Allah the Fairest of all judges?
  96,1,"Read in the Name of your Lord, Who created (everything)."
  96,2,He created human being from a leech-like mass (clinging to the endometrium of the uterus).*
  96,3,"Read, and your Lord is the Most-Generous,"
  96,4,"Who taught (to write) by the pen,"
  96,5,Who taught human being what he did not know.
  96,6,"No, indeed, human being becomes rebellious,"
  96,7,when he thinks he is self-sufficient.
  96,8,"Indeed, to your Lord is the return."
  96,9,"Have you noticed the one who prevents,"
  96,10,an (esteemed) servant (of Ours) when he prays?*
  96,11,"Tell me, if he (i.e. the one who prevents) had been on the right path,"
  96,12,and encouraged (people) to be God-conscious (would it not have been better for him)?
  96,13,"Tell me (now), if he has rejected (the truth) and turned away (from it, would that not be worse for him)?"
  96,14,Does he not know that Allah sees (his conduct)?*
  96,15,"No, indeed! If he does not stop, We shall grab him by the lock of hair over his forehead,"
  96,16,"a lying, sinful forehead."
  96,17,Then let him call his comrades (for help).
  96,18,We will call the guards of Hell.
  96,19,"No, indeed! Do not care about his doings and continue prostrating and drawing near (to Allah)."
